<title>SWITZERLAND: Spector sees aquisitions boosting profit.</title>
<headline>Spector sees aquisitions boosting profit.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian Spector Photo Group NV said the integration of Porst, Spector and Interdiscount France should result in a rise of in annual pre-tax profit of about 400 million Belgian francs.</p>
<p>After the capital increase the anticipated profit rise would amount to a profit before taxes of 90 Belgian francs per spector share, Spector said in a statement released at a news conference in Zurich.  </p>
<p>Spector has agreed to acquire Porst and Interdiscount France from Distefora Holding, previously known as Interdiscount Holding AG.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
